ID: vr-64
Title: Diagnose intermittent native head shutdown delays

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: Post-M1 reliable resource release
Dependencies: vr-45, vr-58

Purpose:
  Explain intermittent owned-head shutdown stalls before claiming reliable
  prompt process, descriptor and memory release during repeated real use.

Tasks:
  Retain exact owned host/compositor/worker identities and phase timestamps.
  Reproduce bounded create/speech/cancel/close cycles with synthetic fixtures.
  Attribute renderer, speech worker, server and desktop cleanup waits.
  Fix only a demonstrated cause and retain unchanged ownership boundaries.

Acceptance criteria:
  Preserve failed receipts; no masking through larger timeouts or blind retries.
  Distinguish an unavailable API from a terminated owned process.
  Verify descriptors, descendants and mutable profile cleanup on success/failure.
  Do not drive or terminate user/sibling apps or call an unknown cause fixed.
  Compare the same close threshold before/after any causal correction.

Completion evidence:
  Prior vr-57 native sessions02 retained an unexplained structural-head close
    timeout; unchanged sessions03 passed. During vr-58 qualification,
    .local\qualification\blink-sessions-01\session-report.json retained a
    20-second native MPFB close timeout and unavailable descriptor inventory.
    Separate blink-sessions-02 passed the unchanged gate for every head, CLI,
    manager exit and parent death. This is intermittent, not a proved blink
    regression, solved failure or permission to change shutdown semantics.

Completion log:
  2026-11-21 - Recorded from actual retained qualification failures. Diagnostic
    attribution and any lifecycle correction remain planned.
